{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion","id":1530497,"title":"How powerful is the Mythos in Scion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-10T16:16:51-08:00","id":1530497,"title":"How powerful is the Mythos in Scion?","content":"I'm thinking they're more powerful than your average gods, but less powerful than the average Primodial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T13:14:12-08:00","id":1530584,"title":"","content":"The most powerful Mythos beings are primordials. Yog-Sothoth and Asathoth are definitely primordials. Cthulhu or Nyarlathotep are probably only around the power level of a senior deity. Some mythos beings are supposed to be rather weak compared to the gods but scary powerful to mortals. Nyarlathotep should be able to intimidate a powerful Pantheon. But he wouldn't want to fight one. Cthulhu isn't someone Thor or Kali would want to fight without serious backup. But Cthulhu wouldn't want to face them without backup either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-11-2024, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T19:21:05-08:00","id":1530600,"title":"","content":"Is that your head Canon, or is it what the book said? From the impression I get from the book is that the Mythos are generally more powerful than the gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T06:01:30-08:00","id":1530635,"title":"","content":"There really isn\u2019t a canon answer to the question.In game terms the Mythos gods are tier 4 characters just like the gods and titans of the various divine pantheons. In my opinion several of the Mythos knacks are highly destructive compared to divine knacks of the same calling, so in that sense maybe they are more powerful. But only if you look at power as a means to do harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T11:38:22-08:00","id":1530659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion?p=1530600#post1530600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that your head Canon, or is it what the book said? From the impression I get from the book is that the Mythos are generally more powerful than the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm comparing my knowledge of Lovecraft with my knowledge of Scion and making my best judgment. Yog-Sothoth is coextensive with all reality. That sounds like a primordial to me. Meanwhile Cthulhu can be trapped in a drowned city, that doesn't sound like an almighty deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T20:02:09-08:00","id":1547292,"title":"","content":"I started the players off in a Iron Setting (Origin level) with lean on action movie tropes. As they have finally met the Divine parents and ascended to Hero status, they have come across artifacts (Status of Y'Golonac) and strange happenings that, while they have managed to come out unscathed by the skin of their teeth, they really know something is off.<br /> <br /> That the Divine parents have chosen not to comment on the subject makes the characters nervous. <br /> <br /> The Mythos should be handled just as vague and mysterious as it is in a regular CoC game.<br /> <br /> The Mythos cares not for Human or Divine preconceptions of morality as it is cosmic indifference in a multi-dimensional form. Which will drive most self-absorbed/self-regarding types mad.<br /> <br /> Use it sparingly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-28T18:46:29-08:00","id":1547297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion#post1530497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking they're more powerful than your average gods, but less powerful than the average Primodial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just treat them as a Pantheon of strange and alien Gods, but not necessarily more powerful than all other Pantheons. The whole &quot;unstoppable, incomprehensible eldritch&quot; thing is dangerous to mortals, sure, but most Gods just chalk it all up as the Mythos' pantheonic quirk. At most, they do have the raw power to be ranked among some of my World's high-tier Pantheons, but lack the structure and cohesiveness that similarly strong Pantheons have.<br /> <br /> They didn't make any actual appearance though. Once signs of a second Titanomachy began to appear, the Theoi, the Aesir, the Teotl, and the Tzevaot (Abrahamic) declared the Mythos as space Titans and formed a begrudging alliance to take them out before any of them could make any move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T07:07:22-08:00","id":1547331,"title":"","content":"While I don't own the book (yet) my gut reaction is that they're roughly on the level of other Pantheons (although I'd potentially run them as a 'young' one who reconned themselves into existence after Lovecraft's birth). They <i>can</i> be difficult to counter due to not running on exactly the same rules as everyone else, but that also makes it harder for their World-based schemes to get off the ground. If they even have any of those, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T20:30:12-08:00","id":1558008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion#post1530497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking they're more powerful than your average gods, but less powerful than the average Primodial.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the Mythos, the very universe itself is just one of Azathoth's dreams. If he were to ever awaken, our universe would instantly blink out of existence.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but he is so anathema to reality, that his very existence causes a rapid fire chain reaction of Big Bangs to trigger around him.<br /> <br /> The guy is mass producing and destroying whole universe, just by sitting there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 01-29-2026, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T20:39:13-08:00","id":1558009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion?p=1530659#post1530659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm comparing my knowledge of Lovecraft with my knowledge of Scion and making my best judgment. Yog-Sothoth is coextensive with all reality. That sounds like a primordial to me. Meanwhile Cthulhu can be trapped in a drowned city, that doesn't sound like an almighty deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cthulhu isn't a deity, he's a high priest. Also, if I'm not mistaken, Hastur (the King in Yellow) is his brother?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion?p=1530635#post1530635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But only if you look at power as a means to do harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the whole point behind the idea of cosmic horror. Existential nihilism, in which the gods (or whatever we recognize as such) are just utterly apathetic towards mortals. The Mythos is not trying to protect us. They're just going about their business, and if they should happen to do something that benefits us in some way, it's just a happy accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 01-29-2026, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T02:50:26-08:00","id":1558016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion?p=1558008#post1558008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the Mythos, the very universe itself is just one of Azathoth's dreams. If he were to ever awaken, our universe would instantly blink out of existence.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but he is so anathema to reality, that his very existence causes a rapid fire chain reaction of Big Bangs to trigger around him.<br /> <br /> The guy is mass producing and destroying whole universe, just by sitting there.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of Scion, that's bog-standard Primordial stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T09:36:55-08:00","id":1558023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion?p=1558016#post1558016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the context of Scion, that's bog-standard Primordial stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Using my knowledge of Greek mythology, I believe the Titans are meant to be living realms (Tartarus, Gaia, est), while the Primordials are meant to be living concepts (Chaos, Darkness, est).<br /> <br /> Azathoth being a representation of pure chaos and destruction would place him within the classsification of a Primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T08:52:32-08:00","id":1558072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion?p=1558023#post1558023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Using my knowledge of Greek mythology, I believe the Titans are meant to be living realms (Tartarus, Gaia, est), while the Primordials are meant to be living concepts (Chaos, Darkness, est).<br /> <br /> Azathoth being a representation of pure chaos and destruction would place him within the classsification of a Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Scion, &quot;Primordial&quot; encompasses both of these things, while &quot;Titan&quot; is a general term for &quot;a God who is opposed to the main Gods&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T21:53:58-08:00","id":1558088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530497-how-powerful-is-the-mythos-in-scion?p=1558072#post1558072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Scion, &quot;Primordial&quot; encompasses both of these things, while &quot;Titan&quot; is a general term for &quot;a God who is opposed to the main Gods&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. There are Titans who are deemed benign enough in their activities, that the Gods don't have any problem with them.<br /> <br /> Effectively taking on a &quot;you don't bother us, we don't bother you&quot; stance on the situation.<br /> <br /> Those who actively oppose the Gods are participants in the second Titanomachy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}